Subject: [PATCH 02333/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1
 (HEADLINE; SETTLE the in-generation moat) -- BUILD a DiNa-LRM-style
 LEAK-ROBUST partial-state reward scorer (arXiv:2602.11146 VERIFIED). .400
 (exp4325) found the .399 in-generation moat did NOT replicate because the
 exp4292 partial-state scorer LEAKED on a 2nd corpus
 (scorer_leak_recheck_passed=false): it recovered answer-bearing cells from
 position cues rather than genuinely scoring the masked denoising state.
 ROOT-CAUSE FIX (DiNa-LRM, 2602.11146 'Beyond VLM-Based Rewards:
 Diffusion-Native Latent Reward Modeling'): a timestep-conditioned reward head
 trained DIRECTLY on noisy/masked DiffusionGemma canvases (noise-calibrated
 uncertainty, inference-time noise ensembling), NOT a post-hoc scorer that
 peeks at clean cells. HARD GATE: the scorer must stay ORACLE-DISTINCT UNDER
 ANSWER-CELL MASKING on >=2 oracle-distinct corpora -- with the answer cells
 masked, the reward signal must NOT recover the answer (collapses to chance on
 the masked-answer probe) AND must still rank partial states by genuine
 process quality. Emit scorer_leak_audit_passed BARE bool := (the scorer
 SURVIVES the masked-answer leak audit on BOTH corpora: no answer recovery +
 non-degenerate process ranking). Deliverable: the persisted scorer module +
 the leak-audit artifact. verifier_is_oracle=false. If NO leak-robust scorer
 can be built (it always leaks or always degenerates) ->
 scorer_leak_audit_passed=false + honest_verdict
 complete_no_leak_robust_partial_state_scorer (decision-grade: the
 partial-state-scoring direction is not viable, retire). NO TRM training;
 DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary.

